<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  BullionEdge Pro — sitemap.

  One entry, because the app genuinely is one page: the router moves between
  views with the fragment (#desk, #risk, #journal), and a fragment is not a URL
  a crawler can index separately. Listing them would be listing this same page
  eight times.

  BullionEdge_Pro.html is deliberately absent. The build writes it as a
  byte-identical copy of index.html for the double-click case, and both carry a
  canonical pointing here, so it must not be advertised as a second page.

  A sitemap may only contain URLs at or below its own directory, which is why
  this one lives inside /bullionedge-pro/ and lists only URLs from there. Submit
  it in Search Console at:
      https://bullionedgepro.github.io/bullionedge-pro/sitemap.xml

  Bump <lastmod> when the page's visible content changes, not on every rebuild —
  a date that moves for no reason teaches Google to stop trusting it.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://bullionedgepro.github.io/bullionedge-pro/</loc>
    <lastmod>2026-08-13</lastmod>
    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
    <priority>1.0</priority>
  </url>
</urlset>
